  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $S,$ so we will treat the other variables $V$ and $R$ as constants. We can use the multiplication principle to solve for $S.$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{SR}{3} \\\\ 3V & =\\frac{3SR}{3} \\\\ 3V & =SR\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3V & =SR \\\\ \\frac{3V}{R} & =\\frac{SR}{R} \\\\ \\frac{3V}{R} & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $S=\\frac{3V}{R}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $R\\ne 0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
